<html>
<head>
	<title></title>
</head>
<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},
<p>Thank you for contacting Qantas Customer Care about your journey to {{{Case.Arrival_City__c}}}&nbsp;on {{{Case.Actual_Arrival_Date_Time__c}}}.</p>

<p>We’re committed to getting you to your destination on time. However, issues outside of our control, such as weather, natural disasters or technical problems can cause flight delays and cancellations.<br />
<br />
When this happens, we understand how inconvenient schedule changes are and know how important it is to let you know straight away.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If notified by QF, use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
I can see that we sent you an email on<em><strong> &lt;date&gt;</strong></em> advising you of the schedule change.<br />
<br />
While we will do our best to provide you with clear and timely information, I’m sorry that we didn’t meet your expectations this time.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If requesting compensation and has been notified, add:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re here to help</strong><br />
<br />
As you were notified within a reasonable timeframe, we’re unable to meet your request for a refund for unexpected expenses on this occasion.<br />
<br />
While these expenses may not be covered by Qantas, your travel insurance policy might be able to cover these sorts of situations.<br />
<br />
Please let me know if you’d like me to provide you with an insurance letter to assist with a claim – we're here to help.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>If not notified by QF, use:</em></strong><br />
<br />
<strong>We’re sorry you weren’t notified</strong><br />
<br />
I’m sorry to hear that you weren’t notified about your flight change. I can understand how frustrating that must have been.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that I’ve provided feedback to the relevant team so they can review their notification processes.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If requesting compensation and was not notified by QF, add:</strong></em><br />
<br />
We'll need you to fill in this <a href="https://qantas.my.salesforce.com/sfc/p/#900000010OOK/a/2v000000ITtV/RTJ8g0c5a3zjzwkf3UVinv1MZAb1Gaqcy_Nakv7ASIA">Customer Care Payment Form</a> and include your receipts for any expense incurred due to the schedule change. We’ll then review your expenses and process your reimbursement as soon as possible.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If not notified by travel agent, use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Contact your travel agent</strong><br />
<br />
Our systems can see that the notification of the flight change was sent to &lt;travel agent&gt; on &lt;date&gt;. This means you’ll need to get in touch with your travel agent regarding any unexpected expenses you incurred due to the change.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>If customer wants to know why there was a schedule change, use:</strong></em><br />
<br />
<strong>Flight scheduling is affected by a huge variety of operational factors.</strong><br />
<br />
As each aircraft in our fleet operates across multiple routes, and any change can have an impact across our entire network, it is not always possible to identify a specific reason for each schedule change.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-if a frequent flyer and providing goodwill gesture</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’ve credited {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account. You can use the points towards flights, food and wine through Qantas Wine, as well as a range of products from Qantas Marketplace.<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-if not a Frequent Flyer and providing goodwill gesture</strong></em><br />
<br />
I’d like to arrange a credit of {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to you. If you’re not already a member, you can join free of charge using this <a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/frequent-flyer/join/code/familyfree">link</a>.<br />
<br />
You can use the points towards flights, food and wine through Qantas Wine, or a range of products from Qantas Marketplace. You can let us know what your Frequent Flyer number is by replying to this email, so we can credit these points to your account as soon as possible.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion&nbsp;</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with an exceptional experience from start to finish.<br />
<br />
Thank you for taking the time to tell us about your experience and I hope we deliver an exceptional service next time you fly with Qantas.</p>
</body>
</html>